    "description": "<p>Dataset produced by paper \"Ousiometrics: The essence of meaning aligns with a power&ndash;danger&ndash;structure framework instead of valence&ndash;arousal&ndash;dominance\" by Dodds et al.</p>\n<p>Scores for words in a three dimensional space of essential meaning.</p>\n<p>Tab-separated columns are:</p>\n<p>1. &nbsp;n-gram (mostly individual words)</p>\n<p>2. Goodness (vs Badness)</p>\n<p>3. Power (vs Weakness)</p>\n<p>4. Aggression (vs Gentleness)</p>\n<p>5. Danger (vs Safety)</p>\n<p>6. Structure (high is unstructured, low is structure)</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The GPAD circumplex lies in the first two dimensions.</p>\n<p>Structure is the third dimension.</p>\n<p>Two minimal orthogonal frameworks are:&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Goodness-Aggression-Structure (GAS)</p>\n<p>Power-Danger-Structure (PDS)<br><br>Power-Danger-Structure aligns with real word usage (tokens), and aligns an array of other systems.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Primary plane is spanned by GA or PD frameworks.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Connection:</p>\n<p>Power = 1/sqrt(2) ( Goodness + Aggression)</p>\n<p>Danger = 1/sqrt(2) (-Goodness + Aggression) = 1/sqrt(2)(Badness + Aggression)</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
